            "mimeType": "text/event-stream",
            "text": "data: {\"type\":\"start\",\"messageId\":\"57a98e23-da9a-4450-9f7a-81d0aa663e7b\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"tool-input-start\",\"toolCallId\":\"think_d7aba627-af5d-46d5-b84c-a7f8a7e688fd\",\"toolName\":\"think\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"tool-output-available\",\"toolCallId\":\"think_d7aba627-af5d-46d5-b84c-a7f8a7e688fd\",\"output\":{\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"text-start\",\"id\":\"57a98e23-da9a-4450-9f7a-81d0aa663e7b\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"text-delta\",\"id\":\"57a98e23-da9a-4450-9f7a-81d0aa663e7b\",\"delta\":\"That\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"text-delta\",\"id\":\"57a98e23-da9a-4450-9f7a-81d0aa663e7b\",\"delta\":\"'s wonderful, Yaniv. What's\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"text-delta\",\"id\":\"57a98e23-da9a-4450-9f7a-81d0aa663e7b\",\"delta\":\" on your mind today?\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"text-end\",\"id\":\"57a98e23-da9a-4450-9f7a-81d0aa663e7b\"}\n\ndata: {\"type\":\"data-citations\",\"data\":[{\"id_uuid\":\"Why Overthinking Can Be Linked to Sensory Processing Issues #mentalhealthawareness\",\"title\":\"Why Overthinking Can Be Linked to Sensory Processing Issues #mentalhealthawareness\",\"meta_data\":{\"url\":\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=Qo54LpYjG7k\",\"video_id\":\"Qo54LpYjG7k\",\"hide_citation\":false,\"raw_transcription_s3_url\":\"https://delphi-training-content-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/2c9b839d-b4bf-47fd-9814-a6f00a2fd6a8/2406e41a-a5af-4284-9c1e-1d8929ac33d1/transcription.json\",\"chunk_title\":\"Overthinking and Sensory Processing Issues\",\"end\":44873,\"start\":112},\"content_type\":\"YOUTUBE\",\"summary\":\"\",\"edited_time\":\"2026-04-16 09:39:00.680728+00:00\",\"created_time\":\"2026-04-15 18:10:06+00:00\",\"text\":\"[SHARI B. KAPLAN, LCSW]: If you have some kind of processing problem like dyslexia or an auditory processing or an ocular motor or any other sensory processing problem, your brain might overthink for you. So mindfulness, journaling, breathwork, or some somatic grounding exercises can be helpful, like going outside and sticking your feet in grass, or as silly as this may sound, tree hugging can be very grounding. So therapy helps to uncover the root cause that's driving these patterns of overthinking. Using EMDR and Internal Family Systems and ego state work along with self-regulation tools is a great way to get to the underlying root cause.\"},{\"id_uuid\":\"Body scan reading.m4a\",\"title\":\"Body scan reading.m4a\",\"meta_data\":{\"hide_citation\":false,\"raw_transcription_s3_url\":\"https://delphi-training-content-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/2c9b839d-b4bf-47fd-9814-a6f00a2fd6a8/8767b65f-30d1-4309-9c29-fed0f4283e0a/transcription.json\",\"end\":679690,\"start\":1840},\"content_type\":\"AUDIO_FILE\",\"summary\":\"\",\"edited_time\":\"2025-10-19 20:59:31.941415+00:00\",\"created_time\":\"2025-10-19 20:40:47+00:00\",\"text\":\"[SHARI B. KAPLAN, LCSW]: Now that we've collected some information on your strengths and how you've processed through some challenging experiences, we're going to help you with a few skills. These skills will help you to connect your feelings to where you experience them in your body. So feelings in your body are also known as emotions or the latest term coined somatic experiences. So this will be important Step three for you as once you know where you're experiencing emotions, feelings or tension in your body, then we can teach you how to be comfortable with these sensations and also learn how to regulate them so that they can be easier for you to experience. Let's begin. Your feelings or emotions may be trapped in your body because of anxiety and fear that you may have experienced in the past and that you may be reminded of, or your body's being reminded of in your current life situation. So many people don't even realize that these emotional traps exist. So once we can locate and identify the feelings in your body, you will learn how to have a relationship with them that will allow you to feel more calmer and more energized, allowing you to be more in charge of making choices in your day to day life. First, you'll be learning how to body scan. Usually a body scan will help you learn where emotions live in your body, where they tend to be trapped, where you feel the tension, the location may change from situation to situation, or you may just have one place that you tend to hold you your emotions in your body. So first I want you to find a comfortable position. Sitting or lying down, gently close your eyes if you feel comfortable doing so. If not, you can also gaze down towards the floor at an angle like approximately 40 to 45 degrees. So if you think of looking down towards the tip of your nose, so keep your head straight and then look down towards approximately a 45 degree angle towards the floor. And this will help you feel the sensations that you're looking to locate and regulate. So now you're going to take a deep breath in through your nose and imagine that breath going down the center of your spine to your tailbone, bringing the breath back up. Now you're exhaling through your spine, through the center of your brain and out through the top of your head. Let's do that again. You're going to inhale your breath in. Imagine it going to the center of your brain, then going down your spine. Then when you get to your tailbone, you exhale back up through your spine, through the center of your brain and out through the top of your head. Let's do that one more time, take a breath in through your nose, into the center of your brain, down your spine, to your tailbone, exhaling back up through your spine, through the center of your brain and out through the top of your head. Okay, now let's start at the top of your head. Slowly bring your attention down through your body like a light is scanning and moving down your forehead, the back of your head, down through your eyebrows and eyelids, your cheeks and nose, your jaw. And notice if things. If your tongue is relaxing in your mouth, if your jaw is tense, just allow the light or the energy to help you notice where there's tension is. Is it feeling warm and tingly and relaxed or are you feeling tension? So, breathing nice and deep, nice and relaxed. Moving down through your neck, the front and the back of your neck, through your shoulders. That's it. Breathing nice and deep, exhaling and relaxing. As the light continues to flow down, scanning your arms, your shoulders, your biceps, your triceps, your forearms, then your wrists, into the palms of your hands and out through your fingertips. Any tension anywhere, just be. Just notice. Allow yourself to keep breathing nice and deep, exhaling and relaxing, Going back to your chest and your upper back. See if there's any tension there. As the light continues to flow down through your abdomen and your middle back. Checking in, noticing any tension you may feel. Breathing nice and deep, exhaling and relaxing. As the light continues to flow down through your pelvic area and your lower back, noticing any tension you may feel your hips and buttocks continuing to breathe deep and relaxed. The light continues through the front of your thighs, the back of your thighs. Notice if there's any tension the outside of your thighs. Breathing nice and deep, exhaling and relaxing. As the energy or light continues to flow down through your knees, your shins, your calves, the tops of your feet and the soles of your feet. Notice any tension you may feel and allow the light to go out through your toes. That's it. Just take a nice deep breath and exhale. Now let's take a moment and just be breathe. Go back through your body and see where you feel relaxation. Now, where you feel tension, is it in your head, your neck? That's it. Just breathing, nice and relaxed. Do you feel anything in your shoulders, your chest, your stomach? Check your hips out and your legs. Now go to where you're feeling the tension if you're feeling tension. And just go to the tense area and try to find what emotions you might feel so you might be able to put your hand on your chest if you feel it on your chest or your neck, maybe your face, your stomach. Be aware when you put your hand there and you're breathing nice and relaxed, do you feel any emotions arise? Any anger or agitation? Frustration, fear? When you breathe into it, do you. Is it releasing? Is there peace? So let's just start in one area. When you find the tension and the sensation, ask yourself, what color is this? First color that comes to your mind. What shape is. Could be a black bob or a red square. Take a breath. If it could talk, what would it say? It might just say shut up. It might have another word or a phrase. It could say something mean or frustrating. Could request for help. Just breathe into it. Just take a nice deep breath and exhale longer than your inhale. You want your exhale to be longer than your inhale. How intense is this feeling? On a scale of 1 to 10, 10 being the most tense and just sit and see what happens. If you breathe the breath that we did at the beginning of the exercise, in through your nose, into the center of your brain, down your spine, to your tailbone, exhaling back up through your spine and out through the top of your head, does the tension seem to release? Acknowledge each emotion as best as you can without judgment. Just simply observe and see if you can release the tension just by observing it. Putting your hand there and doing the breath work. You can repeat this on all the areas of your body that you feel tense. And this is a way to self regulate and also identify. Because once you know where the tension and the emotions live, this is this. This is good to be able to calm down so that it doesn't fuel. Because the calmer you are with your emotions, the more you can take control of your thoughts. So we want to learn how to self regulate our emotions so we can take charge of our thoughts. So first we need to know where they are and what they are. And then we can learn what negative beliefs fuel them so that we can work on repairing that and building in new beliefs that serve you well in your life today. So taking a nice deep breath one more time, in through your nose, into the center of your brain, down your spine, to your tailbone, exhaling back up through your spine, through the center of your brain and out through the top of your head. That's it. So when you're done with this exercise, when you're doing it on your own, you can take one final deep breath and gently open your eyes and return yourself to the awareness in the room. Just take a look around you to get grounded into your surroundings. And remember, there's no right or wrong way to feel. This exercise is all about building awareness of your mind body connection. And now you can understand what we mean by mind body. Because your emotions living in your body and experiencing them while you're having thoughts makes it infinitely important for us to know what beliefs are fueling our emotions and our thoughts. So, becoming comfortable with different body sensations, as well as being able to regulate these emotions, you can start being in charge of not only your thoughts, but your reactions and your behaviors.\"},{\"id_uuid\":\"AI info 4.m4a\",\"title\":\"AI info 4.m4a\",\"meta_data\":{\"hide_citation\":false,\"raw_transcription_s3_url\":\"https://delphi-training-content-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/2c9b839d-b4bf-47fd-9814-a6f00a2fd6a8/f7da8838-f432-4422-b853-49891a8021fe/transcription.json\",\"end\":2075040,\"start\":2054710},\"content_type\":\"AUDIO_FILE\",\"summary\":\"\",\"edited_time\":\"2025-10-19 21:01:22.658531+00:00\",\"created_time\":\"2025-10-19 20:30:46+00:00\",\"text\":\"[ADELANA DON DRUCKER]: Feel grounded? When I am helping people, I feel grounded. When I'm teaching, I feel grounded. When I'm talking about business, Good. When I'm moving my body at the gym, Good. When I play the piano sometimes. But that's not grounded. That's actually in a spiritual, self actualized.\"},{\"id_uuid\":\"AI info 4.m4a\",\"title\":\"AI info 4.m4a\",\"meta_data\":{\"hide_citation\":false,\"raw_transcription_s3_url\":\"https://delphi-training-content-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/2c9b839d-b4bf-47fd-9814-a6f00a2fd6a8/f7da8838-f432-4422-b853-49891a8021fe/transcription.json\",\"end\":3392500,\"start\":3390340},\"content_type\":\"AUDIO_FILE\",\"summary\":\"\",\"edited_time\":\"2025-10-19 21:01:22.658531+00:00\",\"created_time\":\"2025-10-19 20:30:46+00:00\",\"text\":\"[ADELANA DON DRUCKER]: Yeah. All right. Thank you.\"},{\"id_uuid\":\"AI info 3.m4a\",\"title\":\"AI info 3.m4a\",\"meta_data\":{\"hide_citation\":false,\"raw_transcription_s3_url\":\"https://delphi-training-content-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/2c9b839d-b4bf-47fd-9814-a6f00a2fd6a8/3ea05daa-f049-4bef-a499-595a7117d001/transcription.json\",\"end\":1742540,\"start\":1732060},\"content_type\":\"AUDIO_FILE\",\"summary\":\"\",\"edited_time\":\"2025-10-19 21:02:01.189612+00:00\",\"created_time\":\"2025-10-19 20:30:03+00:00\",\"text\":\"[SHARI B. KAPLAN, LCSW]: Right. And he is giving you approval today and he is giving you loving support today. So things have changed.\"},{\"id_uuid\":\"Get Cannectd EP 2: Dr. Antonello Banchi & Shari B. Kaplan LCSW\",\"title\":\"Get Cannectd EP 2: Dr. Antonello Banchi & Shari B. Kaplan LCSW\",\"meta_data\":{\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rf3uM1AhLsk\",\"video_id\":\"rf3uM1AhLsk\",\"hide_citation\":false,\"raw_transcription_s3_url\":\"https://delphi-training-content-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/2c9b839d-b4bf-47fd-9814-a6f00a2fd6a8/c3cf777b-12da-4f82-b2a0-4ab7194427c2/transcription.json\",\"end\":20480,\"start\":16720},\"content_type\":\"YOUTUBE\",\"summary\":\"\",\"edited_time\":\"2025-10-19 20:08:36.627682+00:00\",\"created_time\":\"2024-12-26 17:14:24+00:00\",\"text\":\"[SHARI B. KAPLAN, LCSW]: So I just wanted to say good morning and hello and how are you?\"},{\"id_uuid\":\"Shari B. Kaplan LCSW & Dr Jeffery Ditzell Share Secrets That Can Transform Your Life.\",\"title\":\"Shari B. Kaplan LCSW & Dr Jeffery Ditzell Share Secrets That Can Transform Your Life.\",\"meta_data\":{\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g0sEpw_gb10\",\"video_id\":\"g0sEpw_gb10\",\"hide_citation\":false,\"raw_transcription_s3_url\":\"https://delphi-training-content-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/2c9b839d-b4bf-47fd-9814-a6f00a2fd6a8/3631f8c1-630b-42b7-8976-c4dcc2535be7/transcription.json\",\"end\":3026640,\"start\":3020800},\"content_type\":\"YOUTUBE\",\"summary\":\"\",\"edited_time\":\"2025-10-19 20:16:31.250455+00:00\",\"created_time\":\"2024-12-11 15:29:21+00:00\",\"text\":\"[DR. JEFFREY DITZEL]: Yeah, I'd love to. And again for you, please don't hesitate to contact me anytime, anytime you need anything.\"},{\"id_uuid\":\"Shari B. Kaplan LCSW & Dr Jeffery Ditzell Share Secrets That Can Transform Your Life.\",\"title\":\"Shari B. Kaplan LCSW & Dr Jeffery Ditzell Share Secrets That Can Transform Your Life.\",\"meta_data\":{\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g0sEpw_gb10\",\"video_id\":\"g0sEpw_gb10\",\"hide_citation\":false,\"raw_transcription_s3_url\":\"https://delphi-training-content-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/2c9b839d-b4bf-47fd-9814-a6f00a2fd6a8/3631f8c1-630b-42b7-8976-c4dcc2535be7/transcription.json\",\"end\":3172210,\"start\":3163410},\"content_type\":\"YOUTUBE\",\"summary\":\"\",\"edited_time\":\"2025-10-19 20:16:31.250455+00:00\",\"created_time\":\"2024-12-11 15:29:21+00:00\",\"text\":\"[SHARI B. KAPLAN, LCSW]: Thank you. That's very sweet of you. I appreciate it. Thank you. Have a wonderful day. Bye. Bye.\"},{\"id_uuid\":\"Shari B. Kaplan LCSW & Dr Jeffery Ditzell Share Secrets That Can Transform Your Life.\",\"title\":\"Shari B. Kaplan LCSW & Dr Jeffery Ditzell Share Secrets That Can Transform Your Life.\",\"meta_data\":{\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g0sEpw_gb10\",\"video_id\":\"g0sEpw_gb10\",\"hide_citation\":false,\"raw_transcription_s3_url\":\"https://delphi-training-content-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/2c9b839d-b4bf-47fd-9814-a6f00a2fd6a8/3631f8c1-630b-42b7-8976-c4dcc2535be7/transcriptio